{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPX7yZ29cuMtx8vu6Yix","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`ard setup --create-gh-app` is implemented and the Go tests pass. `make lint` and `make docs-check` did not pass, and I did not run the full `make lint test` in one go. `go test ./...` and `go vet` pass, and the setupcmd, cli and github tests also pass with `-race`.\n\n- **`make lint`:** it reports a gofmt parse error in a file under `internal/roles/testdata`. I didn't touch that file.\n- **`make docs-check`:** it can't run here because `mkdocs` isn't installed, so the docs edit is unchecked.\n\nThe flow builds the manifest from one built-in permission list (no `workflows`, no `administration`). It serves a one-shot form on 127.0.0.1, checks `state` and exchanges the code. It writes the key as a mode-0600 file, refusing an existing path unless `--force`. It then prints the install link and the `ARD_GITHUB_*` lines and runs the normal setup checks. The new flags are `--create-gh-app`, `--app-name`, `--key-file` and `--force`. The getting-started page now leads with the new command and keeps the manual path as a fallback.\n\nThings to know before merging:\n- **1Password:** the opt-in write is not implemented; the plan allowed deferring it.\n- **Permission check:** the setup permission check is still the placeholder from #302. `CheckPermissions` is shared with the manifest and tested against it, but nothing reads the App's granted permissions yet.\n- **`--dry-run`:** it makes one read-only GET to look up whether the owner is a user or an org, so it can print the right URL. It creates nothing and writes no key.\n- **github package:** I added two exported helpers to `internal/github/auth.go` (`DiscoverInstallation`, `DefaultAPIBaseURL`), because the architecture test only allows the API host inside that package.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/350/worker-engineer.md`, and the core code is in `internal/setupcmd/createapp.go`. The callback server and key handling are the security-sensitive parts and are worth a close review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1328,"cache_read_input_tokens":50802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1328},"output_tokens":686,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e831d755-0305-4792-92c3-10bc757b9430","uuid":"d16b13c5-0854-4b06-9cbb-d2bbd40ce0cc","timestamp":"2026-11-25T10:52:28.962Z","request_id":"req_011ChPX7yPqvzxwiS2FpGAkP"}
